## Multi-Machine Sync

**Machines:** {{PRIMARY_MACHINE}} (primary) + {{OTHER_MACHINES}} (secondary)

```bash
# PRIMARY: created/updated a skill -> push brain
ai-push "added skill: my-new-skill"

# SECONDARY: pull latest brain + sync to project
ai-pull                     # pull ~/.claude/ + sync all projects
ai-pull {{ARM_1}}           # pull + sync only one arm
ai-pull --status            # check if updates available
```

### Active Projects (registered in sync-ai-docs)

```
{{ARM_1}}, {{ARM_2}}
```

### First-Time Setup on a New Machine

```bash
git clone {{YOUR_REPO_URL}} ~/.claude
cp ~/.local/bin/sync-ai-docs ~/.local/bin/
cp ~/.local/bin/ai-pull ~/.local/bin/
cp ~/.local/bin/ai-push ~/.local/bin/
chmod +x ~/.local/bin/{sync-ai-docs,ai-pull,ai-push}
ai-pull   # sync everything
```

## Client Onboarding

When creating a new client arm:

```bash
mkdir ~/path/to/<CLIENT_CODE>
cd ~/path/to/<CLIENT_CODE>
git init
# Create .claude/CLAUDE.md from templates/arm/CLAUDE.md.template
# Create .github/copilot-instructions.md (sync target)
# Register in sync-ai-docs
sync-ai-docs <CLIENT_CODE>
```

Then add to:
1. `company/COMPANY.md` Arms table (this file)
2. `company/config/arms.json` (connectome arm definitions)
3. `~/.config/querymaster/connections.json` (DB connections)

